99 +26,280 =30,879\n\n30,879 +525,600 =556,479\n\nWait, but let me check with another method. 657×800 is indeed 525,600. 657×40=26,280. 657×7=4,599. Adding those together: 525,600 +26,280 =551,880 +4,599 =556,479. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, 657×847 =?\n\nAlternatively, use standard multiplication:\n\n   657  \n×847  \n--------\nFirst, 657 ×7 = 4,599\n\nThen 657 ×40 = 26,280 (shifted one position)\n\nThen 657 ×800 =525,600 (shifted two positions)\n\nAdding:\n\n4,599  \n26,280 → total so far: 30,879  \n525,600 → total is 556,479. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 556,479.\n\nWait, but in my initial thought process I was confused with different numbers, but upon redoing it properly, it's clear. So the template needs to be filled with:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 657 and 847?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 847 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 657 by the ones place digit 7 of 847: 657 ×7 = 4,599.\n2. Multiply 657 by the tens place digit 40 of 847: 657 ×40 = 26,280.\n3. Multiply 657 by the hundreds place digit 800 of 847: 657 ×800 =525,600.\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 4,599 +26,280 +525,600 =556,479.\nSo, the final computed product is 556,479.\n\nYes, that should be correct. I think the confusion earlier was because I was mixing up numbers from different problems, but now I've fixed it. So the final answer is 556,479.", '']
