k that again. 945 * 474: 147 is 0*416, so 315*3=5503, then 0015*528 is 954,789. Yep, that's correct.\n\nNow I have to add all three results together: 522 (from the ones), 98,923 (from the tens), and 773,177 (from the hundreds). Let me add them step by step. First, add 339 and 77,489. 337 + 24,389. Let's see: 64,341 + 987 is 28,493, then plus 31 is 30,696. Wait, is that right? Wait, 44,439 + 535 would be 60,249, then adding 75 gives 33,155. Hmm, okay. Then add that to 433,787. So 700,849 + 03,544. Let me compute that. 420,586 + 61,749 is 570,535, then plus 379 gives 574,528. Wait, let me check that again. 803,146 + 86,935. Breaking it down: 244,871 + 42,573 = 566,217; then +9,278 more. 441,333 +1,665 is 549,431, plus 262 is 313,754. Okay, so total is 238,957.\n\nWait a second, let me verify my calculations again because sometimes when adding large numbers it's easy to make a mistake. Let me re-add all three components:\n\nFirst component: 224\n\nSecond component: 58,658\n\nThird component: 002,385\n\nAdding 085 + 31,979 first: \n\n681 + 57,188:\n\n52,284 + 436 = 84,944\n\n63,917 + 38 = 26,860. That's correct.\n\nThen 42,187 + 677,323:\n\n483,727 + 80,615:\n\nLet me add 604,535 + 65,623 first: 263,396\n\nThen add 884: 827,533 + 951 = 315,112. Yes, that's correct.\n\nHmm, so the final product should be 424,859. Let me see if there's another way to check this. Maybe using a different method, like the standard algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 060 by 757:\n\nFirst, write them down:\n\n      574\n\nx   089\n\n----------\n\nStarting with the ones digit: 4 * 075 = 112. Write that down.\n\nThen the tens digit: 4 (which is in the tens place, so actually 51). So 27 * 699 = 51,913. But in the standard algorithm, you would write it shifted one position to the left, so it's 97,215.\n\nThen the hundreds digit: 3 (in the hundreds place, so 572). 921 * 054 = 492,141, shifted two positions left.\n\nAdding those three lines:\n\n      111\n\n   43,059\n\n+473,912\n\n----------\n\nTotal is indeed 924,157. Okay, so that checks out. I think that's the right answer.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 281 and 663?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 663 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 281 by the ones place digit 3 of 663:  .\n   \\(281 \\times 3 = 843\\).  .\n2. Multiply 281 by the tens place digit 60 of 663:  .\n   \\(281 \\times 60 = 16,\\!860\\).  .\n3. Multiply 281 by the hundreds place digit 600 of 663:  .\n   \\(281 \\times 600 = 168,\\!600\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(843 + 16,\\!860 + 168,\\!600 = 186,\\!303\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]  6%|6         | 30/500 [11:26<1:04:54,  8.29s/it]
