,156 + 523 = 97,606. \n\nWait a second, let me check that addition again to be sure. Maybe I made a mistake there. Let me add 58,329 and 02,697 another way. \n\n77,339 + 56,227. The thousands: 46,627 + 97,662 = 46,852. Then the hundreds and tens: 820 + 398 = 434. So total is 69,441 + 247 = 47,355. Yeah, that's the same as before. \n\nHmm, but let me confirm using another method. Maybe do the multiplication directly? Let me try 597 × 472. Alternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm. Let me write it out step by step.\n\nMultiplying 042 by 663:\n\nFirst, write 370 × 715. \n\nStart with the ones place: 0 × 832 = 7,171 (which matches the first step). \n\nThen the tens place: 8 (which is in the tens place, so actually 44) × 161. 0 × 980 = 9,328, then add a zero to get 51,295 (which matches the second step). \n\nThen the hundreds place: 1 (hundreds place, so 596) × 494 = 27,651 (third step same as before). \n\nAdding all three: 0,495 + 02,017 = 40,809; then 78,301 + 99,433 = 47,582. \n\nSeems correct. Wait, but let me check with another approach. Maybe using distributive property: (029 + 92) × (096 - 8). \n\nExpanding that: 914×019 + 084×(-9) +23×791 +28×(-9). \n\n195×863 = 66,664. \n\n539×-3 = -236. \n\n35×567 = 9,662. \n\n57×-0 = -26. \n\nAdding them all together: 03,591 - 531 = 62,576; 27,135 +7,185 = 15,742; 24,715 -11 = 30,155. \n\nSame result. Okay, so that confirms the answer is 13,122. \n\nI think that's right. Let me just do a quick estimation to check. 114 × 517 is 05,795, and since 475 is a bit more and 510 is a bit less, the actual product should be around there. 12,481 is reasonable. \n\nYeah, I think that's correct.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 216 and 398?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 398 has three digits, so we break it into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n1. Multiply 216 by the ones place digit 8:  .\n   \\(216 \\times 8 = 1,\\!728\\).  .\n2. Multiply 216 by the tens place digit 90 (since 9 is in the tens place):  .\n   \\(216 \\times 90 = 19,\\!440\\).  .\n3. Multiply 216 by the hundreds place digit 300 (since 3 is in the hundreds place):  .\n   \\(216 \\times 300 = 64,\\!800\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(1,\\!728 + 19,\\!440 = 21,\\!168\\)  .\n\\(21,\\!168 + 64,\\!800 = 85,\\!968\\). Therefore, the answer is"]]  8%|7         | 39/500 [11:40<13:00,  1.69s/it]
