rent numbers because I was solving a different problem (maybe confused with the template example). But following the correct problem step-by-step, it should be 338,826. Let me confirm using another method.\n\nAlternative method: 758 ×447 = 758 ×(400 + 40 +7) = 758×400 +758×40 +758×7, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, compute using another approach:\n\n758 ×447:\n\nLet me compute 700×447 = 312,900.\n\nThen 58×447:\n\n58×400 = 23,200\n\n58×40 =2,320\n\n58×7 =406\n\nSo 23,200 +2,320 =25,520; +406 =25,926.\n\nTotal: 312,900 +25,926 =338,826. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 338,826.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 758 and 447 is \\boxed{338826}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 758 and 447, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 758 by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 7 = 5306\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 758 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 40 = 758 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3032 \\times 10 = 30320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 758 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 400 = 758 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 3032 \\times 100 = 303200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   5306 + 30320 + 303200\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(5306 + 30320\\):\n     \\[\n     5306 + 30320 = 35626\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(303200\\):\n     \\[\n     35626 + 303200 = 338826\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 758 and 447 is \\(\\boxed{338826}\\).", '']
