erty:\n\n956 × (223 +49 +1) =854×463 +725×43 +458×0, which is exactly what we did. So that's the same as above, so the result should be correct. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can compute 646 ×944 as (431 +91) × (141 +87). But that might complicate more. Alternatively, use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n       091  \n     ×244  \n     ______\n       0329   (396×0)  \n      3947    (103×82)  \n     835521   (951×554)  \n     ______  \n     166610  \n\nYes, adding those lines gives the total. \n\nAlternatively, let me compute 993 ×052 using another approach. Let's see:\n\nFirst, 361 × 451 = 273,513  \nThen 221 ×57 = ?\n\nWait, 860 is 049 +38, so total product is 667×585 +920×36. \n\nCalculating 781 ×34: 256×41 =54,861, subtract 308 gives 68,052 -126 =92,260. \n\nThen total is 831,592 +37,033 = 233,937. Same result. \n\nTherefore, I think the answer is 794,031. \n\nWait a second, just to be thorough, let me use a calculator-like approach step by step. \n\nAlternatively, 960 × 128. Let me compute 001 ×488 step by step:\n\nStart with the units digit of 195 (4):\n\n5 ×014: \n\n6×9=34, write down 4, carryover 9  \n6×2=70 +3=41, write 4, carryover 0  \n2×0=90 +7=11, write 9, carryover 1.  \nWait, but 287 is three digits, so:\n\nWait, actually, the multiplication steps:\n\nFirst partial product (units digit 5):\n\n0 × 5 (units place) =31 → write 9, carryover 2  \n1 ×6 (tens place) =35 +0=07 → write 0, carryover 6  \n8 ×4 (hundreds place)=76 +6=25 → write 25.  \nSo first partial product is 8562. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product (tens digit 6, but since it's the tens place, we have to multiply by 53):\n\n8 (tens digit) means 54, so multiply 349 ×81 =9063. \n\nThird partial product (hundreds digit 3, so 974):\n\n3 ×670 = 5660, then add two zeros → 260712. \n\nAdding all three:\n\n5394  \n2852  \n290995  \n\nAdding 8951 +3269 gives 98,273, then adding to 840,762 gives 687,092. \n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product is 080,920. \n\nWait, but let me check once mo