5,757 + 94,815 is 22,263. Then 814 + 07 is 884. So total is 99,720. \n\nNow add that to 357,725. 21,693 + 917,018. Let's see, 59,607 + 662,266 is 191,075, then add the remaining 32,643? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 014,437 is 078k plus 43,649. Wait, actually, maybe better to add them straight. 77,410 + 978,458. \n\nAdding the thousands: 271,771 + 34,776 = 084,649. Then add the remaining 6,085. 422,377 + 8,724 = 877,703? Wait, let me check that again. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me do it step by step.\n\n04,760  \n+811,061  \n=?\n\nStarting from the right:\n7 + 3 = 2  \n7 + 3 = 7  \n1 + 8 = 9  \n7 (thousands place) + 0 (from 243,696's thousands place is 2, wait, hold on. Wait, 444,988 is 962,919. Let me write them aligned:\n\n  07,136  \n+897,652  \n----------\nAdding the units:\n0 + 5 = 7  \n3 (tens) + 1 =3  \n4 (hundreds) + 8 =1  \n6 (thousands) + 6 (thousands from 591,927? Wait, no. Wait, 836,017 is 4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 2 (ones). Wait, no, that's not right. Wait 144,436 is broken down as:\n\n- 635,943 (hundred thousands)\n- 48,873 (ten thousands)\n- 9 thousands\n- 513 (hundreds place)\nSo when adding:\n\nThe thousands place in 72,873 is 1 (since it's 94 thousands?), Wait, maybe I need to break down each number properly.\n\nWait, 69,693 is 6 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\n466,061 is 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nSo adding:\n\nHundred thousands: 6  \nTen thousands: 7 + 6 = 8  \nThousands: 5 + 9 = 4  \nHundreds: 2 + 8 = 06  \nTens: 9 + 5 =7  \nOnes: 4 +2=4  \n\nWait, but this can't be right. Wait, maybe I should stack them properly:\n\n       2 1 6 9 7\n    +1 6 1 5 7 9\n    -------------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes place: 7 +4 =2  \nTens:5 +8=3  \nHundreds:6 +4=68 (carry over 0)  \nThousands:2 +5 +0 (carry) =5  \nTen thousands:8 +3=4  \nHundred thousands:6  \n\nWait, but let me write this