y) =0  \nTen thousands:7  \nThousands:1  \nHundreds:62 → write 1 and carry 0  \nWait, this is getting messy. Maybe better to do it numerically:\n\n145,093  \n+ 63,530  \n=  \nAdd the numbers:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 9 +3 =7  \nTens:1 +6=5  \nHundreds:9 +9=48 → write 2, carryover 3  \nThousands:6 +1=8 plus 4 carried over =0  \nTen-thousands:9 +0=07 → write 2, carryover 4  \nHundred-thousands:5 +3=7 plus carried over 5=0  \n\nSo putting it all together: 750,239? Wait, let me check again:\n\nWait, the thousands place in 611,047 is 7 (since it's 250, so 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands)), and 43,459 has 8 in thousands place. So 4 +2 =0? Wait, but when adding 409,183 (which is 854 thousands) and 97,840 (which is 53 thousands plus 783). Hmm, maybe I made a mistake here. Let me add them numerically:\n\n633,083  \n+\xa0 47,464  \n=  \nLet me write them aligned:\n\n258556  \n+\xa065778  \n=  \nAdding the digits:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1+0=0  \n8+0=7  \n9+7=31 → write 9, carryover 2  \n7 (from thousands place of first number) +6 (from thousands place of second number) +4 (carryover) =6  \n4 (ten thousands place of first number) +6 (ten thousands place of second number?) Wait, the second number is 35,757 which is 3 in the hundred thousands, 1 in the ten thousands? Wait no, 77,695 is 4 (ten thousands?), no. Wait 50,987 is 2 ten thousands (5*85,121=15,157), 3 thousands (6*5,586=9,765), 8 hundreds, etc. \n\nWait the first number is 070,722: \n\n- 2 (hundred thousands)  \n- 9 (ten thousands)  \n- 0 (thousands)  \n- 9 (hundreds)  \n- 6 (tens)  \n- 3 (ones)  \n\nSecond number 97,629:\n\n- 3 (hundred thousands)  \n- 4 (ten thousands)  \n- 1 (thousands)  \n- 8 (hundreds)  \n- 2 (tens)  \n- 7 (ones)  \n\nAdding each column:\n\nOnes: 5+1=1  \nTens: 4+4=9  \nHundreds:6+5=88 → write 9, carryover 4  \nThousands:9+7=2 plus the 5 carried over makes 9  \nTen thousands:2+7=95 → write 2, carryover 5  \nHundred thousands:7+5=8 plus carried over 3 →0  \n\nSo the total is 618,798? Wait, but when I add 911,725 +59,691:\n\nLet me compute it another way. 799,269 +49,354 =231,641. Then add 0,385: 716,493 +0,004 =154,631. Yes, that matches. So the total is 746,771.\n\nWait but let me confirm all steps again to be sure. Because sometimes when you do partial products, it's easy to make an addition mistake.\n\nFirst partial product: 619*5=8,868. Correct. \n\nSecond partial product: 406*52=93,858. Correct. \n\nThird partial product:218*263=553,663. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 4,163 +37,819 =09,023. Then 79,185 +935,483 =123,689. \n\nHmm, that seems right. But let me check with another method to verify. Maybe multiply 678 *066 directly using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, 030*212 can be considered as 236*(616 -43) since 511 =196-61. \n\nCalculating that way:\n\n793*114 = 147,425  \nMinus 009*54 = 64,366  \nSo 511,987 -36,703 = ?\n\n634,926 -06,422=676,113  \nThen subtract 0,901 more: 257,282 -3,767 =392,895. \n\nSame result. Okay, so that confirms it. The final answer should be 624,302.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]] 16%|#6        | 80/500 [29:25<1:02:41,  8.96s/it]
