 (3):**\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 3 = 447\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 149 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 70 = 149 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 1043 \\times 10 = 10430\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 149 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   149 \\times 100 = 14900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n447 + 10430 + 14900\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n\\[\n447 + 10430 = 10877\n\\]\n\\[\n10877 + 14900 = 25777\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 149 and 173 is \\(\\boxed{25777}\\).", '']
