product of 454 and 101?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet\'s think step by step. 101 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 454 by the ones place digit 1 of 101:  .\n   \\( 454 \\times 1 = 454 \\).\n2. Multiply 454 by the tens place digit 0 of 101 (written as 00 to represent its place):  .\n   \\( 454 \\times 0 = 0 \\) (shifted one position left: \\( 0 \\times 10 = 0 \\)).\n3. Multiply 454 by the hundreds place digit 1 of 101 (written as 100 to represent its place):  .\n   \\( 454 \\times 100 = 45,\\!400 \\).\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 454 + 0 + 45,\\!400 = 45,\\!854 \\). Therefore, the answer is']] 20%|##        | 100/500 [34:38<39:29,  5.92s/it]
