ep. 894 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three parts:.\n1. Multiply 242 by the ones place digit 4:  .\n   \\(242 \\times 4 = 968\\).  .\n2. Multiply 242 by the tens place digit 90 (since \\(9 \\times 10 = 90\\)):  .\n   \\(242 \\times 9 = 2178\\), then append a zero to get \\(21,\\!780\\).  .\n3. Multiply 242 by the hundreds place digit 800 (since \\(8 \\times 100 = 800\\)):  .\n   \\(242 \\times 8 = 1936\\), then append two zeros to get \\(193,\\!600\\).  .\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(968 + 21,\\!780 + 193,\\!600 = 216,\\!348\\).  .\n\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is"]] 21%|##1       | 107/500 [35:48<31:52,  4.87s/it]
