f 745 (which is 700 + 40 + 5):\n\n1. Multiply 325 by the ones place digit (5):\n   \\[\n   325 \\times 5 = 1625\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 325 by the tens place digit (40), which is 4 in the tens place:\n   \\[\n   325 \\times 40 = 325 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 1300 \\times 10 = 13000\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 325 by the hundreds place digit (700), which is 7 in the hundreds place:\n   \\[\n   325 \\times 700 = 325 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 2275 \\times 100 = 227500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1625 + 13000 + 227500\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 1625 and 13000:\n\\[\n1625 + 13000 = 14625\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 227500:\n\\[\n14625 + 227500 = 242125\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 325 and 745 is \\(\\boxed{242125}\\).",
