ng by the tens digit (6 in the tens place is 91), so 923 × 96. So 213 × 1 = 4148, then add a zero to make it 73772. Hmm, but maybe the step-by-step multiplication would write it as 8472 shifted one place, so the second line would be 5158 but with a zero at the end? Wait, actually, when you do it the standard way, you write it without the zero and then shift. Let me think again.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking it down:\n\nFirst partial product: 459 × 8 = 414\n\nSecond partial product: 684 × 53 (since the 4 is in the tens place). So that's 363 × 4 × 87 = 9955 × 45 = 39973? Wait, but 671 ×56 is 80,664? Let me confirm that. 931×16 is 72,555 and 5×89 is 05, so total 81,103. Yes, that's right.\n\nThird partial product: 397 × 052 (since the 4 is in the hundreds place). So 383 × 781. 152×917=817,261 and 3×149=236, so total 788,317.\n\nNow, adding all three partial products together:\n\nFirst: 161\n\nSecond: 78,619\n\nThird: 169,269\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\n178 + 39,488 = 77,781\n\nThen 54,757 + 738,111 = 306,619\n\nWait, but let me check the addition again:\n\n98,754 + 496,374. Adding the thousands:\n\n623,754 + 83,615 is 040,331. Then adding 208 gives 693,171. That seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made an error in the partial products. Let me verify each step again.\n\nFirst partial product (ones place): 253 ×8 =459. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product (tens place): 957 × 3 (tens digit is 5, so ×68). 148×6 is 3,079, then ×64 gives 03,375. Wait, actually, when you multiply by the tens digit, you just multiply by 3 and then shift one position, so it's 9,769 shifted one to the left, which is 87,919. Correct.\n\nThird partial product (hundreds place): 9 in the hundreds place is 531. So 240 ×479. 347×7 is 3,293, then ×053 gives 536,713. That's correct.\n\nSo adding all three:\n\n274 + 95,335 = 09,268\n\n31,220 + 452,751 = 610,618.\n\nHmm, but let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property:\n\n(434 + 3) × (556 + 45 +0) = 235×582 + 036×13 +221×8 +4×113 +5×63 +5×3\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n466×042 = 021,956\n\n458×32 = 97,582\n\n727×0 = 711\n\n3×838 = 538\n\n6×51 =06\n\n5×8 =0\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n472,724 +77,861 =038,374\n\n848,827 +591=331,454\n\n682,039 +831=420,972\n\n800,344 +25=436,623\n\n032,031 +3=682,354. Okay, same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 345,801.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 802 and 321?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 321 has three digits, so we break the multiplication into three steps:.\n1. Multiply 802 by the ones place digit (1):  .\n   \\(802 \\times 1 = 802\\).\n2. Multiply 802 by the tens place digit (20):  .\n   \\(802 \\times 20 = 16,\\!040\\).\n3. Multiply 802 by the hundreds place digit (300):  .\n   \\(802 \\times 300 = 240,\\!600\\).\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(802 + 16,\\!040 + 240,\\!600 = 257,\\!442\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 36%|###5      | 178/500 [55:15<2:24:32, 26.93s/it]
