final_output:  ["366,429.\n\nWait, hold on, this is getting confusing. Let me start over properly. The user's question was the product of 555 and 971, but in my thinking process, I messed up the numbers. Let me correct that.\n\nWait, the user provided:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 555 and 971?\n\nSo the correct numbers are 555 and 971. I need to compute 555 × 971.\n\nAlright, let's do this step by step.\n\nFirst, break down 971 into its place values: 900 + 70 + 1.\n\nMultiply each part by 555, then add the results.\n\nStep 1: 555 × 1 (ones place) = 555\n\nStep 2: 555 × 70 (tens place) = 555 × 7 × 10 = 3,885 × 10 = 38,850\n\nStep 3: 555 × 900 (hundreds place) = 555 × 9 × 100 = 4,995 × 100 = 499,500\n\nNow sum all three results:\n\n555 (step1) + 38,850 (step2) + 499,500 (step3)\n\nFirst, add 555 + 38,850:\n\n555 + 38,850 = 39,405\n\nThen add 39,405 + 499,500:\n\n39,405 + 499,500 = 538,905\n\nWait, but let me confirm this addition:\n\n39,405 + 499,500:\n\nAdd the thousands:\n\n39,405 is 39,000 + 405\n\n499,500 is 499,500\n\nAdding 39,000 + 499,500 = 538,500\n\nThen add 405: 538,500 + 405 = 538,905. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, using another method:\n\n555 × 971 can also be calculated as 555 × (1000 - 29) = 555,000 - (555 × 29)\n\nCompute 555 ×29:\n\n555 ×30 = 16,650\n\nSubtract 555: 16,650 - 555 = 16,095\n\nSo total product: 555,000 -16,095 = 538,905. Same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 538,905.\n\nBut looking back at my initial incorrect thinking process, I had gotten confused with different numbers but ended up with 366,429 which is wrong. So the correct answer is 538,905.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 555 and 971 is \\boxed{538905}.", '']
