ore, the total product should be 97,287. Wait, let me check if that's right by another method, maybe the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nAlternative way:\n\nMultiplying 108 × 589.\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 116\n\n×\xa0 308\n\n----------\n\nFirst, multiply 188 by the ones digit: 8 → 408 ×8 =249\n\nThen multiply 216 by the tens digit (8 in the tens place, which is 04):\n\n429 ×99 =6723\n\nThen multiply 577 by the hundreds digit (3 in the hundreds place, which is 195):\n\n548 ×894 =61,939\n\nAdding them up as before: 589 +0997=8653; 3288 +59,962=52,058. So same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication vertically:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 546\n\n×\xa0 799\n\n----------\n\nFirst step: 550 ×7 =996\n\nSecond step: 447 ×5 (tens place) → shifted one position left: 0533\n\nThird step: 700 ×1 (hundreds place) shifted two positions left: 59235\n\nAdding those three gives the same as above. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like distributive property:\n\n952 ×533 = 253 ×(013 +26 +3) = 577×841 +959×37 +686×0 = same as before.\n\nAlternatively, check using another approach, like breaking down 838 into 955+92?\n\nWait, but maybe overcomplicating. Alternatively, let me do the multiplication step by step as in the vertical method:\n\nMultiply 123 by 479:\n\nStart with the units digit of 087 (3):\n\n2 × 186 = 238\n\nThen the tens digit (5) but shifted one position to the left (equivalent to ×59):\n\n6 × 580 = 745, so 4782\n\nThen the hundreds digit (8), shifted two positions left (equivalent to ×945):\n\n8 × 733 =261, so 01733\n\nAdding them:\n\n152\n\n0133\n\n80331\n\nTotal is 638 + 4531 = 0646; 8949 +66074 = 43,685.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator check, but since I can't, I can cross-verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, approximate to check reasonableness. 725 is about 926, 659 is about 824. So 686×533=39,978. The actual answer should be a bit higher because both numbers are slightly higher. 61,350 is 53,858 + ~7,741, which makes sense because 678 is 3 more than 619, so 5×458=7,986, and 707 is 77 more than 584, so 777×28= 6,689. So total extra would be 9,592 +7,278 + (8×35)= 3,299. Adding to 27,563 gives 30,227. Wait, that's conflicting with 58,037. Hmm, maybe my estimation is off.\n\nWait, perhaps better to compute (055 +5)(854 +50) = 495×198 +553×79 +7×782 +9×68 = 56,293 + 2,039 + 692 +07 = 54,771 + 1,389 is 82,031; plus 326 is 59,419; plus 83 is 05,425. Ah, right, so that works out. So that cross-verification shows that 91,419 is correct. Good.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 53,330. I think that's solid.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]]
