+ 39,950 = 45,543 (since 5,593 + 39,950: 5,000 +39,000 =44,000; 593+950=1,543 → total 45,543).\n\nThen add 399,500: 45,543 + 399,500.\n\nAdding 45,543 + 399,500:\n\n45,543 + 400,000 = 445,543, but subtract 500 (since it was 399,500 instead of 400,000) → 445,543 -500 = 445,043.\n\nWait, let me check that again:\n\n399,500 +45,543:\n\n399,500 +40,000 =439,500  \n439,500 +5,543 = 445,043.\n\nYes, so total sum is 445,043.\n\nTherefore, the product of 799 and 557 is 445,043.\n\nWait, let me verify with another method to be sure. Let\'s compute 799 ×557 using another approach, perhaps the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   799  \n×557  \n--------\nFirst, multiply by 7 (ones place):\n\n799 ×7 = 5,593 (matches step 1)\n\nNext, multiply by 5 (tens place, so actually 50):\n\n799 ×5 =3,995, then shifted one position to the left: 39,950 (matches step 2)\n\nNext, multiply by 5 (hundreds place, so 500):\n\n799 ×5 =3,995, shifted two positions left: 399,500 (matches step 3)\n\nAdding all three:\n\n5,593  \n39,950  \n399,500  \n--------\nAdding 5,593 + 39,950 = 45,543  \n45,543 + 399,500 = 445,043. \n\nSame result. Alternatively, let me compute using (800 -1) × (500 +50 +7):\n\nExpand using distributive property:\n\n800×500 +800×50 +800×7  \n-1×500 -1×50 -1×7\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n800×500 = 400,000  \n800×50 =40,000  \n800×7 =5,600  \n-1×500 = -500  \n-1×50 = -50  \n-1×7 = -7  \n\nNow add them all together:\n\n400,000 +40,000 =440,000  \n440,000 +5,600 =445,600  \n445,600 -500 =445,100  \n445,100 -50 =445,050  \n445,050 -7 =445,043.\n\nPerfect, that\'s the same answer. So the final product is indeed 445,043.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 799 and 557 is \\boxed{445043}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 799 and 557?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet\'s think step by step. The number 557 has three digits, so we can break down the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 799 by the ones place digit 7 of 557:\n   \\[\n   799 \\times 7 = 5593\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 799 by the tens place digit 50 of 557 (since 5 is in the tens place):\n   \\[\n   799 \\times 50 = 39950\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 799 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 557 (since 5 is in the hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   799 \\times 500 = 399500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n5593 + 39950 + 399500 = 445043\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{445043}.', ''] 47%|####6     | 233/500 [1:12:42<2:42:56, 36.61s/it]
