 2 = 440\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 220 by the tens place digit (80) of 682:\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 80 = 220 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 1760 \\times 10 = 17600\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 220 by the hundreds place digit (600) of 682:\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 600 = 220 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 1320 \\times 100 = 132000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n440 + 17600 + 132000 = 440 + 17600 = 18040\n\\]\n\\[\n18040 + 132000 = 150040\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 220 and 682 is \\(\\boxed{150040}\\).", '']
