es 7 = 4242\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \n     - \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\) (write down 2, carry over 4)\n     - \\(0 \\times 7 + 4 = 4\\)\n     - \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\) (write down 2, carry over 4)\n     - Final carry over 4.\n\n2. **Multiply 606 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   606 \\times 90 = (606 \\times 9) \\times 10 = 5454 \\times 10 = 54540\n   \\]\n   - Calculation:\n     - \\(6 \\times 9 = 54\\) (write down 4, carry over 5)\n     - \\(0 \\times 9 + 5 = 5\\)\n     - \\(6 \\times 9 = 54\\) (write down 4, carry over 5)\n     - Final carry over 5.\n\n3. **Multiply 606 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   606 \\times 700 = (606 \\times 7) \\times 100 = 4242 \\times 100 = 424200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   4242 + 54540 + 424200 = 482982\n   \\]\n\nVerification using an alternative method:\n- Compute \\(606 \\times 797\\) as \\(606 \\times (800 - 3)\\):\n  \\[\n  606 \\times 800 = 484800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 606 \\times 3 = 1818\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  484800 - 1818 = 482982\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 606 and 797 is \\(\\boxed{482982}\\).",
