732. So the final answer should be 261,023. \n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method, like using the distributive property:\n\n620 × 707 = 329 × (487 + 78 +7) = 989×766 +383×08 +800×7, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 556×351 directly:\n\nAlternatively, using another approach:\n\nLet me compute 434×358 = 268,334\n\n918×55 = 955×79 +085×4=55,173 +9,691=25,755\n\n28×311=16,215\n\n88×15=2,394\n\n9×492=058\n\n0×42=60\n\nAdding all together: 475,161 +43,335 = 607,372; 641,436 +21,467=904,922; 509,417 +6,809=220,005; 121,413 +659=724,338; 595,793+70=333,031. Yep, same result. So that seems correct. \n\nI think that's solid. So the product is 934,591.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 761 and 526?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 526 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:.\n1. Multiply 761 by the ones place digit (6):  .\n   \\(761 \\times 6 = 4,\\!566\\).  .\n2. Multiply 761 by the tens place digit (20):  .\n   \\(761 \\times 20 = 15,\\!220\\).  .\n3. Multiply 761 by the hundreds place digit (500):  .\n   \\(761 \\times 500 = 380,\\!500\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(4,\\!566 + 15,\\!220 + 380,\\!500 = 400,\\!286\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 50%|#####     | 251/500 [1:21:02<1:27:18, 21.04s/it]
