ep 3: Multiply 114 by the hundreds digit (800):\n\n114 ×800 = 114 ×8 ×100 = 912 ×100 = 91,200.\n\nNow sum all three results:\n\n228 (from step 1) + 7,980 (step 2) = 8,208.\n\n8,208 + 91,200 (step 3) = 99,408.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 99,408.\n\nI need to present this in the template provided, following the example\'s structure. The example had three steps for a three-digit number, so same here. The answer should be 99,408.\n\nI need to make sure that in my explanation I follow the steps clearly and correctly. Let me check the arithmetic again:\n\n114 ×2 is indeed 228.\n\n114 ×70: 114×7 is 798, so ×10 is 7,980.\n\n114×800: 114×8=912, so ×100=91,200.\n\nAdding them: 228 +7,980 = 8,208. Then 8,208 +91,200 = 99,408. Correct.\n\nAlright, so the reasoning should be structured as such.\n</think>', '']
