ich is 1 in 417's tens place), you multiply by 1\u00d7178 and shift one position left (equivalent to \u00d710). So 1\u00d7178=178, shifted left once is 1,780. Then the hundreds digit is 4, so 4\u00d7178=712, shifted two places (equivalent to \u00d7100) gives 71,200.\n\nTherefore, adding them up:\n\n1246  \n1780  \n71200  \nTotal: 1246 + 1,780 = 3,026; 3,026 + 71,200 = 74,226. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding all three:\n\n1246 + 1780 = 3026. Then 3026 +71200 =74,226. Yes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be 74,226. I think my initial mistake was in the first thought process where I confused the numbers, but after redoing it carefully, it's 74,226. Let me check with another method.\n\nAnother way: 178 \u00d7400 =71,200. 178 \u00d717 = 3,026. Then 71,200 +3,026 =74,226. Yep, same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 74,226.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 178 and 417 is \\boxed{74226}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 178 and 417, we break down the multiplication using the standard method:\n\n1. Multiply 178 by the ones place digit (7):\n   \\[\n   178 \\times 7 = 1246\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 178 by the tens place digit (10), shifting one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   178 \\times 10 = 1780\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 178 by the hundreds place digit (400), shifting two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   178 \\times 400 = 71200\n   \\]\n\nAdding all the results together:\n\\[\n1246 + 1780 + 71200 = 74226\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 178 and 417 is \\(\\boxed{74226}\\).",
