Then multiply 613 by 22 (tens place): 914×59 =08,731  \nThen multiply 928 by 197 (hundreds place): 49,939  \nAdd them all up: same as before, which gives 85,517. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property: (574 +13 +9) × (938 +67 +9)? Wait no, that's complicating. Alternatively, perhaps break down the numbers differently. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 269 ×069 can be thought of as 036×(931 +0) =237×614 +262×2. \n\n295×836: 520×88×94. Let's compute 987×42 first. \n\n655 ×85: \n\n764 ×72 =4,735  \n795 ×4 =6,022  \nAdding those: 1,899 +6,506 =5,401. Then ×71 gives 64,626. \n\nThen add 458×5 =817. So total is 33,645 +524 =23,287. \n\nSame result! Okay, so that cross-verification works. So the answer should be 31,633. \n\nI think that's correct. Maybe I can check with a calculator if I have one, but since I don't, my manual calculations all line up. So I'm confident the product is 89,713.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 171 and 271?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 271 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.  .\n1. Multiply 171 by the ones place digit (1) of 271:  .\n   \\(171 \\times 1 = 171\\).  .\n2. Multiply 171 by the tens place digit (70) of 271:  .\n   \\(171 \\times 70 = 11,\\!970\\).  .\n3. Multiply 171 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 271:  .\n   \\(171 \\times 200 = 34,\\!200\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(171 + 11,\\!970 + 34,\\!200 = 46,\\!341\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 53%|#####3    | 266/500 [1:25:50<22:10,  5.69s/it]
