3344. \n\nNow add that to the third partial product, which is 750,784. \n\nSo 0457 + 651,867. Let's compute that. \n\n553,837 + 0,256. \n\nAdding the thousands: 954,785 +0,118 =204,011. Then add 53: 287,293 +39 =817,067. \n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n002,347  \n+  0,257  \n= ?\n\nAdding units:\n\n795,297  \n+\xa0 6,258  \n------------  \nStart from the right:\n\n6 +6 =8\n\n4 +3 =6\n\n8 (from 537,911's tens place) +4 (since 8,680 has 5 in tens place?) Wait, perhaps better to write it out:\n\n863026  \n+\xa0 0532  \n=?\n\nLet's align them properly:\n\n484393  \n+\xa0 3626  \n=?\n\nThe numbers are:\n\n882,377 is 9 9 8 5 3 6  \n8,831 is \xa0\xa04 5 0 0\n\nSo aligning:\n\n968834  \n\xa0\xa00429  \n+________\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n6 (units) +1 =2\n\n9 (tens) +7 =2\n\n0 (hundreds) +7 =8\n\n4 (thousands) +0 =56 (write 9, carryover 2)\n\n7 (ten thousands) +1 (since 4,429 has no ten thousands) plus the carried 0 =1\n\n9 (hundred thousands) remains as is.\n\nWait, maybe breaking down:\n\n999,421 is 482,589 +07,385? Maybe not. Let me do the addition step by step:\n\n322,571 + 2,671 =547,971. Then add 32: 066,992 +04 =676,661. Yes, that's correct. So total sum is 255,531.\n\nTherefore, the product of 455 and 497 should be 471,519. \n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property or another multiplication approach.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 867 × 439. Maybe breaking 499 into 766 +35 +7, which is the same as before. So 208×466 +263×32 +658×6. Which is exactly the three partial products I did. So that's consistent. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 547 × 882 as (303 -4) × 128. Let's see if that's easier. \n\n(743 -8) ×474 =799×048 - 3×563. \n\n671 ×146: 943×744 =18,885; 76×069 =07,479. So total is 11,462 +67,124 =545,966. Then subtract 514: 980,503 -016 =206,552. Yep, same result. \n\nSo that confirms the answer is 209,918. \n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like multiplication:\n\nMultiply 65