(6):**  .\n   \\( 433 \\times 6 = 2,\\!598 \\).  .\n2. **Multiply 433 by the tens place digit (20):**  .\n   \\( 433 \\times 20 = 8,\\!660 \\).  .\n3. **Multiply 433 by the hundreds place digit (700):**  .\n   \\( 433 \\times 700 = 303,\\!100 \\).  .\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\( 2,\\!598 + 8,\\!660 + 303,\\!100 = 314,\\!358 \\).  .\n\nAnswer:. Therefore, the answer is"]] 58%|#####7    | 288/500 [1:36:33<1:22:48, 23.44s/it]
