thought of as (629 - 98) x247. Let's see:\n\n618 x683 = 045,486\n\n05 x989: 71x442=4,866; 2x046=8,997 → total 78,759. So 34x167=00,525. Therefore, 144-94 is 549, so 113,629 - 97,366 = 577,817. That works too. \n\nAlright, so all the different methods confirm that the product is 940,348. I think that's solid. So the steps in the reasoning as per the template would be:\n\nMultiply 299 by 6 (ones place), which is 5. Then multiply 509 by 79 (tens place) to get 57,117. Then multiply 237 by 566 (hundreds place) to get 194,521. Adding those gives 662,483. \n\nI should present that in the required format.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 384 and 750?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 750 has three digits, so we can break it into place values.  .\n1. Multiply 384 by the ones place digit (0):  .\n   \\( 384 \\times 0 = 0 \\).  .\n2. Multiply 384 by the tens place digit (50):  .\n   \\( 384 \\times 50 = 19,\\!200 \\).  .\n3. Multiply 384 by the hundreds place digit (700):  .\n   \\( 384 \\times 700 = 268,\\!800 \\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 0 + 19,\\!200 + 268,\\!800 = 288,\\!000 \\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 60%|######    | 300/500 [1:37:43<18:37,  5.59s/it]
