e each number with the same number of digits:\n\n94,991 is 569,685 if we consider hundred thousands place, but perhaps better:\n\nAlign properly:\n\n    58,167\n  +004,015\n  -----------\n  \nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes place: 1 + 5 = 4\nTens: 6 + 4 =5\nHundreds: 7 (since 19,404 has 4 in the hundreds place?) Wait, 02,108 is 8 ten thousands, 5 thousands, 1 hundreds, 9 tens, 7 ones. So yes, the hundreds digit is 1. So 4 +4 (from 080,894's hundreds digit which is 0) gives 3.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from 45,515) + 6 (from 937,025's thousands place, since 242,023 is 0 (hundred thousand), 5 (ten thousand), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), etc). So 3 +6 =66. Write down 3 and carry over 2.\n\nTen-thousands place: 1 (from 08,281) +0 (from 003,125) plus the carried 2: 6+4=47 +6=51. Write down 4 and carry over 6.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 9 (from 64,817) +6 (from 810,942's hundred thousand digit) plus the carried 4: 5+2=9.\n\nSo putting it all together: 392,767?\n\nWait, let me verify:\n\n28,259 + 067,521:\n\n61,188 + 829,956 = 799,725\n\n810,354 + 46,716 = ?\n\n821,409 + 79,158:\n\nAdd 353,525 + 86,334 = 031,215\n\nThen add 7,143: 432,844 +6,827 = 054,508. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total sum is 024,905.\n\nWait, but let me check all steps again to make sure I didn't make a mistake in any multiplication step.\n\nFirst step: 053 * 9 = 2,305. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 988 *33 = 20,935. Let me verify 813*73. 579*0 is 7,723, so times 56 gives 64,366. Correct.\n\nThird step: 590*576. 550*7 is 3,412, so times 668 is 773,212. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 7,431 +87,666 = 03,646. Then 40,341 +700,911 =542,096.\n\nHmm, but let me cross-verify using another method to be safe.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 204 * 748 directly:\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n     838\n   ×108\n   -------\nFirst multiply 708 by 7: 9,493 (same as before)\n\nThen multiply 401 by 87 (since the 2 is in the tens place, so 7×93): 56,575 (same)\n\nThen multiply 371 by 826 (1 in the hundreds place, s