hould be 161,634. But in my first mistaken thought process, I ended up with conflicting numbers because I was using wrong numbers, but now corrected.\n\nSo the final answer is 161,634. The user's problem is 237 and 682, so the product is 161,634.\n\nWait a second, let me confirm once more with direct multiplication:\n\n237\n\n×682\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 237 by 2: 474\n\nThen multiply 237 by 80 (shift one position to the left):\n\n237 × 80 = 18,960\n\nThen multiply 237 by 600 (shift two positions left):\n\n237 × 600 =142,200\n\nAdding all three:\n\n474\n\n+18,960\n\n=19,434\n\n+142,200\n\n=161,634. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 161,634. I must have made a miscalculation earlier when I thought I got 308,196, but that was due to using different numbers. So now, the correct answer is 161,634.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 237 and 682 is \\boxed{161634}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 237 and 682, we break down the multiplication step by step using the place values of 682:\n\n1. **Multiply 237 by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   237 \\times 2 = 474\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 237 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   237 \\times 80 = 237 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 1896 \\times 10 = 18960\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 237 by the hundreds place digit (600):**\n   \\[\n   237 \\times 600 = 237 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 1422 \\times 100 = 142200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\n\\[\n474 + 18960 + 142200\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n474 + 18960 = 19434\n\\]\n\nThen add the result of the third step:\n\\[\n19434 + 142200 = 161634\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 237 and 682 is \\(\\boxed{161634}\\).", '']
