natively, maybe use a calculator if I can, but since I can't, I'll stick with the step-by-step addition. I think my calculations are correct. So the final answer should be 940,728.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 402 and 843?  .\n# Reasoning:  .\nLet's think step by step. 843 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps.  .\n1. Multiply 402 by the **ones place digit (3)** of 843:  .\n   \\( 402 \\times 3 = 1,\\!206 \\).  .\n2. Multiply 402 by the **tens place digit (40)** of 843:  .\n   \\( 402 \\times 40 = 16,\\!080 \\).  .\n3. Multiply 402 by the **hundreds place digit (800)** of 843:  .\n   \\( 402 \\times 800 = 321,\\!600 \\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\( 1,\\!206 + 16,\\!080 + 321,\\!600 = 338,\\!886 \\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 69%|######9   | 345/500 [1:53:26<1:07:13, 26.02s/it]
