lace value, multiplying, and summing. The initial thought process had a mix-up with different numbers, but upon correcting, the result is consistent.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 440 and 714?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 714 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 440 by the ones place digit 4 of 714:  \n   \\(440 \\times 4 = 1,\\!760\\).\n2. Multiply 440 by the tens place digit 10 of 714:  \n   \\(440 \\times 10 = 4,\\!400\\).\n3. Multiply 440 by the hundreds place digit 700 of 714:  \n   \\(440 \\times 700 = 308,\\!000\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(1,\\!760 + 4,\\!400 + 308,\\!000 = 314,\\!160\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{314160}.",
