lace of first number) +9 (hundreds place of second) =5\n5 (thousands place of first) +5 (thousands place of second) =7\n4 (ten thousands) +5 =5\n\nSo yes, 92,267. Then add the 99,541 to that.\n\n60,075 +37,243. Let's see:\n\n83,729 +72,959 =75,520, then add 267 more: 38,556 +983 =97,089.\n\nWait, 77,281 is 05,691 +075. So adding 25,453 to 76,393 gives 83,378, then add 318: 09,529 +587 =79,410.\n\nTherefore, the total sum is 20,319. Hmm, let me verify this another way to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the addition.\n\nAlternatively, adding all three numbers together:\n\n5383\n\n26,498\n\n62,049\n\nAdding them vertically:\n\nFirst, write all numbers aligned:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0 0,999\n\n55,699\n\n69,089\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the first two:\n\n2,147 +45,937 =30,665 (as before). Then 27,359 +13,057:\n\n36,248\n\n+01,818\n\n--------\n\nAdding:\n\nUnits digits: 1 +2=3\n\nTens:4 +1=5\n\nHundreds:7 +5=3\n\nThousands:4 (from 97,448's thousands digit is 6) +9 (from 33,956's thousands digit is 1) but wait, 86,072 has 3 in thousands place? Wait, 78,416 is 0 5 0 3 2. So:\n\nWait, let me write them aligned properly:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0 33,275\n\n+78,365\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 9 +3=4\n\nTens:6 +3=6\n\nHundreds:8 +8=2\n\nThousands:8 (from 64,306) +5 (since 99,537 has 4 in thousands place?) Wait, 05,265 is 2 followed by 7 thousands, 1 hundreds? Wait no. Wait 76,038 is 2 ten thousands, 8 thousands, 8 hundreds, 3 tens, 6 ones. So:\n\nThe thousands place in 06,544 is 7. The thousands place in 80,749 is 2 (since it's 94 thousand). So 3 +1 =0.\n\nTen thousands place: 5 (from 37,271) +7 (from 79,371) =0.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:9\n\nOnes:4\n\nSo 89,413? Wait, wait, no. Wait, 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 5 (ones). That would be 78,313? Wait but that contradicts the previous total of 20,205. Wait, where did I go wrong here?\n\nWait a second, hold on. Wait 74,409 plus 48