ns place) to get 9,270.\n\nMultiply 103 by 700 (hundreds place) to get 72,100.\n\nSumming them: 412 + 9,270 = 9,682. Then 9,682 +72,100 =81,782.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 81,782.\n\nI need to ensure that the thought process accurately reflects this, correcting any previous errors.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 103 and 794 is \\boxed{81782}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 103 and 794, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 794:\n\n1. **Multiply 103 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 4 = 412\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 103 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 90 = 103 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 927 \\times 10 = 9270\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 103 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 700 = 103 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 721 \\times 100 = 72100\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these partial products:\n\\[\n412 + 9270 = 9682\n\\]\n\\[\n9682 + 72100 = 81782\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 103 and 794 is \\(\\boxed{81782}\\).", '']
