   129168  \n\nYes, that adds up. So the correct answer is 129,168. I think the earlier confusion was because I was looking at a different problem in my mind, but now focusing on the given numbers, it's clear. So the final answer is 129,168.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 312 and 414 is \\boxed{129168}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 312 and 414?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 414 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places for easier multiplication.\n1. Multiply 312 by the ones place digit 4 of 414:\n   \\[\n   312 \\times 4 = 1248\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 312 by the tens place digit 10 (which is 1 in the tens place) of 414:\n   \\[\n   312 \\times 10 = 3120\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 312 by the hundreds place digit 400 (which is 4 in the hundreds place) of 414:\n   \\[\n   312 \\times 400 = 124800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1248 + 3120 + 124800 = 129168\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{129168}.",
