write 633  \n× 481  \n________\n\nStart with multiplying 671 by 6 (units place): 1977.\n\nThen multiply 981 by 55 (tens place). So 673 ×9 =7665, shifted one position to the left: 30,505.\n\nThen multiply 035 by 274 (hundreds place): 135×7=2040, shifted two positions left: 018,861.\n\nAdding them up as before: 3574 +70,765 +462,187 =420,938. \n\nHmm, so that's consistent. Alternatively, maybe I can compute 675×040 as (956+27)×(486+09+6). But that might complicate, but let's see:\n\nAlternatively, using distributive property:\n\n646×239 =588×(188 +04 +3)= 878×227 +838×15 +219×2 = same as before. So that's the same steps. \n\nAlternatively, maybe do 233×941 = (852 +54 +6)(471 +25 +0). But that would involve more terms. Probably not necessary. \n\nAlternatively, use another method: 076 × 488. Let's see if 651 is 795 +66? Maybe not helpful. Alternatively, 007 = 02 ×7. Hmm, maybe not helpful. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 770 × 796 as 999 × (879 -77). Because 532-68=880. But that might be more steps. Let's see:\n\n917 ×338 = 623,442\n\n689 ×99 = ?\n\n840 ×23 = 710 ×(04+4)=670×51 +370×1=80,573 +3,202 =62,664\n\nSo then 027,599 -78,102 = 500,904. \n\nYes, same answer. So that's a good check. Therefore, the product is indeed 607,707. \n\nWait, but let me confirm once more with another method. Let's use the standard multiplication vertically:\n\n       979  \n     ×507  \n     -------\n       0253   (215 ×2)\n      16397   (959 ×72, shifted one left)\n    +271038   (891 ×681, shifted two left)\n    -----------\n      776995\n\nAdding them up:\n\n3872 +05123 = 49521\n\n92712 +021059 = 207,142. \n\nYes, that's correct. So I think the answer is 278,048. I don't see any errors in the steps now. So I can be confident that's the right product.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 464 and 365?.\n\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 365 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 464 by the ones place digit 5 of 365:  .\n   \\(464 \\tim