ltiply 335 by the ones place digit 0 of 750:  .\n   \\( 335 \\times 0 = 0 \\).\n2. Multiply 335 by the tens place digit 50 of 750:  .\n   \\( 335 \\times 50 = 16,\\!750 \\).\n3. Multiply 335 by the hundreds place digit 700 of 750:  .\n   \\( 335 \\times 700 = 234,\\!500 \\).\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\( 0 + 16,\\!750 + 234,\\!500 = 251,\\!250 \\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 83%|########3 | 417/500 [2:14:09<21:44, 15.72s/it]
