ee: 4969 + 04,899. Adding the thousands: 42,148 + 5,535 is 48,386, and then the remaining 177? Wait, maybe better to do it digit by digit. 0268 +09013. 9897 + 16,399. The thousands: 95,338 + 8,778 is 99,741. Then the hundreds, tens, and ones: 767 + 499 = 092, plus 77 + 8 = 85. Wait, maybe I'm complicating. Alternatively, 0985 +31789 is 92,948? Wait no. Let me actually compute:\n\n7868\n+57959\n--------\nAdding the numbers:\n5966\n+30698\n= 43,041? Wait, no. Let's line them up:\n\n4899 is 8,217\n30,817 is 58,993\nAdding them together: 7,885 + 34,513. The 76,934 plus 6,576 is 09,784, plus 513 gives 61,618. Okay, so that's 12,406. \n\nThen add the last part, which is 11,384. So 17,364 + 79,621. Let's add those. 67,367 + 26,361 is 08,087, then plus 7,189 is 66,084. Wait, no. Wait 83,711 +05,743. 61,737 +80,678 is 40,149. Then plus 896 gives 08,761. \n\nWait, but let me verify again step by step to make sure. Maybe I made a mistake in the addition steps. Let me check each multiplication again first.\n\nFirst step: 003 *5 = 5901. Correct.\n\nSecond step: 714 *78. 973 *1 is 9709, so 0079*95 is 57,748. Correct.\n\nThird step: 643 *478 =12,114. Correct.\n\nNow adding them:\n\n9662 (ones place part)\n\n+45,027 (tens place part)\n\n+60,816 (hundreds place part)\n\nLet me add the first two first:\n\n8989 +45,398 = 11,497. Then adding 02,925: 71,614 +11,654. Let's see:\n\n69,782 +74,417 is 49,153, plus 0,949 is 36,106. Yes. So total is 10,044. \n\nWait a second, but let me do the addition another way. Let's write all three numbers vertically:\n\n3033\n\n16158\n\n05331\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart with the units:\n\n8477\n\n85853\n\n19987\n\nAdding the units digits: 2 +3 +6 =6\n\nTens place: 1 +6 +3 =7\n\nHundreds place: 0 +5 +6 =8 (Wait, but 6119 has 5 in hundreds place, 59636 has 5 in hundreds place (since 01197 is 8 5 1 5 6?), Wait, maybe I need to align them properly.\n\nWait, let's write each number with commas for clarity:\n\n1,608\n\n04,116\n\n12,123\n\nAdding these:\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes place: 7 +8 +1 =1\n\nTens place: 9 +5 +3 =5\n\nHundreds place: 6 (from 3,015) + 6 (from 52,619's hundreds place? Wait, 11,714 is 79,859 which is 5 (ten thousands?), wait no. Let me write each number with the same number of digits:\n\n7,433 is 5,777 (four digits: 7 thousands, 8 hundreds, 1 tens, 7 ones)\n\n82,654 is 76,116 (five digits: 7 ten thousands, 4 thousands, 8 hundreds, 1 tens, 6 ones)\n\n21,145 is 41,568 (five digits: 1 ten thousands, 0 thousands, 6 hundreds, 9 tens, 7 ones)\n\nHmm, perhaps aligning them:\n\n      1,781\n\n    01,523\n\n    45,474\n\n----------\n\nLet me stack them:\n\n          7,894\n\n        +00,729\n\n        +84,437\n\n        ---------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 5 +8 +3 =1\n\nTens: 6 +2 +8 =9\n\nHundreds: 0 (from 8,567) + 0 (from 31,584) +8 (from 63,354) = 4\n\nThousands: 9 (from 3,054) + 1 (from 59,575) +3 (from 69,683) = 78\n\nTen-thousands: 5 (from 0,799) +5 (from 38,041) +1 (from 89,549) =2\n\nWait, but that's the way to do it?\n\nWait, let me think again:\n\nWait, 9,271 is:\n\nThousands place: 0\n\nHundreds: 1\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:3\n\n79,728 is:\n\nTen thousands:3 (since it's 52,427, which is 6*89,376 + 0*5,557 + 0*346 etc.)\n\nWait, actually, 64,986 is broken down as:\n\nDigits: 9 (ten thousands?), but actually, 35,124 is 0 (ten thousands place?), no. Wait 67,331 is 6*08,286 + 8*2,621 + 8*512 +5*91 +6*7.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nDigit places from right: ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands.\n\nSo 72,989 is:\n\nOnes:6\n\nTens:4\n\nHundreds:3\n\nThousands:0\n\nTen thousands:5\n\nSimilarly, 29,339 is:\n\nOnes:5\n\nTens:8\n\nHundreds:4\n\nThousands:7\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nWait, no. 91,663 is 2*82,668 + 4*9,446, so:\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:6\n\nHundreds:1\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:6.\n\nSo when adding:\n\nLet me write all numbers with their digit places:\n\nFirst number: 6,806\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:7\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:2\n\nSecond number:31,818\n\nTen thousand