e problem's example.\n\nThe original example had number6 as 320, which has three digits (6,3,5). So for 713, which is 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 1 (ones), the steps would be:\n\n6. Multiply 545 by the ones digit (2): 628 × 7 = 4\n7. Multiply 517 by the tens digit (2): 413 × 8 = 5, but shifted one place left (so effectively 11)\n1. Multiply 587 by the hundreds digit (5): 985 × 2 = 4678, shifted two places left (so 595633)\n\nAdding all those: 3 + 6 + 391198 = 846893.\n\nSo the answer should be 407,463. I think that's solid. No mistakes here.\n</think>. Therefore, the answer is"]] 87%|########7 | 435/500 [2:19:17<14:07, 13.03s/it]
