rt:\n\n206,920 + 6,651 = 213,571  \n\nWait, let me verify the addition step by step:\n\nAdding 147,800 and 59,120:\n\n147,800  \n+ 59,120  \n=  \nStart from the right:  \n0 +0 =0  \n0 +2 =2  \n8 (hundreds place) +1 (hundreds place) =9  \n7 (thousands) +9 (thousands) =16 \u2192 write 6, carryover 1  \n4 (ten thousands) +5 (ten thousands) +1 (carryover) =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1  \n1 (hundred thousands) +0 +1 (carryover) =2  \n\nSo total is 206,920. Correct.\n\nNow adding 6,651:\n\n206,920  \n+\u00a0 6,651  \n=  \nAdding units: 0+1=1  \nTens:2+5=7  \nHundreds:9+6=15 \u2192 write 5, carryover1  \nThousands:6 +6 =12 +1 =13 \u2192 write3, carryover1  \nTen thousands:0 +0 +1 =1  \nHundred thousands:2 remains  \n\nThus total is 213,571.\n\nHmm, but let me confirm with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiply 739 by 289:\n\nSet it up:\n\n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0739  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00d7\u00a0289  \n\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0----------\n\nFirst, multiply 739 by 9 (units place):\n\n739 \u00d79 = 6,651 (as before)\n\nNext, multiply 739 by 80 (tens place):\n\n739 \u00d78 = 5,912 \u2192 then add a zero: 59,120 (matches)\n\nThen multiply 739 by 200 (hundreds place):\n\n739 \u00d72 = 1,478 \u2192 add two zeros: 147,800 (matches)\n\nAdding them:\n\n6,651  \n59,120  \n147,800  \nTotal: 6,651 +59,120 =65,771; 65,771 +147,800 =213,571. So correct.\n\nAlternatively, cross-check with another approach, like using (700 + 39) \u00d7 (200 + 89):\n\nWait, maybe that's complicating. Alternatively, using the difference of squares?\n\nWait, 289 is 17\u00b2, but 739 is a prime? Not sure. Alternatively, perhaps approximate:\n\n700 \u00d7 289 = 202,300  \n39 \u00d7289 = 39\u00d7200 +39\u00d789 =7,800 + 3,471 =11,271  \nTotal: 202,300 +11,271 =213,571. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 213,571. \n