le in mind but then switching to the actual problem. Now it's clear. The final answer is 126,585.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe final computed product is \\boxed{126585}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 435 and 291?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 291 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 435 by the ones place digit (1) of 291:\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 1 = 435\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 435 by the tens place digit (90) of 291:\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 90 = 435 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 3915 \\times 10 = 39150\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 435 by the hundreds place digit (200) of 291:\n   \\[\n   435 \\times 200 = 435 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 870 \\times 100 = 87000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n435 + 39150 + 87000 = 126585\n\\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 435 + 39150 + 87000 = 126585.\nSo, the final computed product is 126585.\n\n\\boxed{126585}", ''] 90%|######### | 450/500 [2:23:29<16:33, 19.87s/it]
