28,584 +397,000 =425,584.\n\nSo the correct answer is 425,584.\n\nI must have initially confused the numbers with another problem, leading to confusion. Let me ensure now that this is correct by another method, like the standard multiplication:\n\n       794\n\n     \u00d7536\n\n     --------\n\n       4764 (794\u00d76)\n\n      23820 (794\u00d730, shifted one position)\n\n     397000 (794\u00d7500, shifted two positions)\n\n    -----------\n\n      425,584\n\nYes, that adds up correctly. Therefore, the final answer is 425,584.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 794 and 536 is \\boxed{425584}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 794 and 536?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 536 has three digits, so we can break it down into 6, 30, and 500.\n\n1. Multiply 794 by the ones place digit 6:\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 6 = 4764\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 794 by the tens place digit 30 (which is 3 \\(\\times 10\\)):\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 30 = 794 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 2382 \\times 10 = 23820\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 794 by the hundreds place digit 500 (which is 5 \\(\\times 100\\)):\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 500 = 794 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 3970 \\times 100 = 397000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4764 + 23820 + 397000 = 425584\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{425584}\\).",
