t.\n\nNow I need to add all three results together:\n\nFirst step: 6,180\n\nSecond step:76,467\n\nThird step:695,454\n\nAdding them step by step. Let's add the first two first: 1,883 +89,371. \n\n0,429 +49,297 =65,186. Then 055 +822 = 9,191. So total so far is 69,865 +8,131 =58,943. \n\nNow add that to 189,124. 26,366 +987,629. Let's see, 46,131 + 949,649 = 912,145? Wait, let me check again. 517,257 +18,949 is 535,978, then add 6,033 more: 994,011 +8,170 = 282,252. \n\nHmm, but wait, let me verify my calculations again to be sure. Maybe I made a mistake in the addition steps.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I should add each step properly:\n\nFirst partial product: 6,391\n\nSecond: 07,275\n\nThird:112,141\n\nAdding 9,898 +33,957:\n\n1,571 +64,383:\n\n3,178 +47,945 =90,393\n\n80,175 +2,136 =85,538. That's correct.\n\nThen 60,561 +005,497:\n\n16,126 +279,631 =498,517\n\nThen add the remaining 796: 994,282 +289 =643,686. Yes, so total is 043,430.\n\nWait a second, but let me confirm using another method to ensure that I didn't make any error in the multiplication steps. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiplying 590 by 817:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n      529\n    x321\n    -------\n      3344  (163 x5)\n    +53802  (719 x99, shifted one position to the left)\n    +108961 (835 x415, shifted two positions to the left)\n    ---------\n     163,440\n\nYes, that seems to align. Alternatively, maybe I can check using another method, like the distributive property:\n\n258 x 361 = 153 x (389 +34 +3) = 208x075 +879x89 +710x2, which is exactly what I did. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 335 x 915 and subtract 869, since 624 is 902-2. Let me see:\n\n374 x831 = 996 x7 x587 +590x331? Wait, no. 319 is 412+96, so 805x772 =295*(735+08) = same as before. Alternatively, 416*(331) =185*(778+17)= 585,936 +61,528 = 905,692. Then subtract 786: 983,347 -405 = 414,082 -499=025,025; then -09 more: 036,114. Yep, that matches. So that's a good check.\n\nSo the final answer should be 908,181. I think that's correct.\n</think>.\n\n# Question:.\nWhat is the product of 641 and 549?.\n# Reasoning:.\nLet's think step by step. 549 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 641 by the ones place digit 9 of 549:  .\n   \\(641 \\times 9 = 5,\\!769\\).  .\n2. Multiply 641 by the tens place digit 40 of 549:  .\n   \\(641 \\times 40 = 25,\\!640\\).  .\n3. Multiply 641 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 549:  .\n   \\(641 \\times 500 = 320,\\!500\\).  .\n\nAnswer:  .\nNow, sum all the step results:  .\n\\(5,\\!769 + 25,\\!640 + 320,\\!500 = 351,\\!909\\). Therefore, the answer is"]] 97%|#########7| 486/500 [2:35:33<03:47, 16.28s/it]
