swer properly in the given template:\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 936 and 121?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 121 has three digits, so we can break it into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 936 by the ones place digit (1): 936 × 1 = 936.\n2. Multiply 936 by the tens place digit (20): 936 × 20 = 18,720.\n3. Multiply 936 by the hundreds place digit (100): 936 × 100 = 93,600.\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 936 + 18,720 + 93,600 = 113,256.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 113,256.\n\nTherefore, the boxed answer should be \\boxed{113256}.\n\nWait, let me verify once more with direct multiplication:\n\n936 × 121:\n\nFirst, 936 × 1 = 936\n\nThen, 936 × 20 = 18,720\n\nThen, 936 × 100 = 93,600\n\nAdding those together:\n\n936 + 18,720 = 19,656\n\n19,656 + 93,600 = 113,256. Yep, that's correct. So the final answer is indeed 113,256. The earlier mistake was due to misreading the original numbers, but now corrected.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 936 and 121?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 121 has three digits, so we can break it into three steps.\n1. Multiply 936 by the ones place digit (1) of 121:  \n   \\( 936 \\times 1 = 936 \\).\n2. Multiply 936 by the tens place digit (20) of 121:  \n   \\( 936 \\times 20 = 18,\\!720 \\).\n3. Multiply 936 by the hundreds place digit (100) of 121:  \n   \\( 936 \\times 100 = 93,\\!600 \\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 936 + 18,\\!720 + 93,\\!600 = 113,\\!256 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is 113,\\!256.\n\n\\boxed{113256}", '']
